    <decisions>
        <description>Only an existing Organization is affiliated. A missing Account, an NPSP Household, or any individual account on the Bucket and one-to-one models is refused with a clear message.</description>
        <name>Switch_Organization</name>
        <label>Switch</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>getContact</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>continue</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Not_An_Organization</name>
            <conditionLogic>or</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>getOrganization</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>getOrganization.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>HH_Account</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>getOrganization.npe01__SYSTEMIsIndividual__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Assign_Not_An_Organization</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Not an Organization</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>WHAT IT DOES: Affiliates a Contact with an Organization Account in NPSP (an npe5__Affiliation__c record) and returns the affiliation&apos;s Id. Running it twice never creates a duplicate: the Contact&apos;s Current affiliation to that Organization is updated instead.

HOW IT WORKS, STEP BY STEP:
1. Reads the Account and refuses anything that is not an Organization. An NPSP Household is never an affiliation: a person joins a Household through their Contact&apos;s Account.
2. Reads the Contact&apos;s current Primary Affiliation.
3. Looks for the Contact&apos;s Current affiliation to this Organization, newest Start Date first. If there is one, its Id rides into the field map, turning the save into an update.
4. Builds the affiliation in the Affiliation (Field Map) transform: the Contact, the Organization, Status Current, the Start Date kept from the existing affiliation (today for a new one), the Role you pass in (or the existing Role when you pass none), and Primary.
5. Primary: the affiliation is marked Primary only when the person has no Primary Affiliation yet, or it already is this Organization. Otherwise the flag is left as it was (not Primary on a new affiliation). NPSP retires a person&apos;s previous primary affiliation (Former, End Date today) whenever a new one is marked Primary, so this rule means a form never closes out someone&apos;s current employer - and a portal user&apos;s primary affiliation, which controls the account they sign in with, is never moved.
6. One Create element set to upsert on Id saves it, insert or update as the map decides.

WHERE IT FITS: The NPSP Contact engine calls this after a person converts when the Add to Account rules (or the capturing section&apos;s Add to Account setting) ask for it and the submission&apos;s Account is an Organization. It is form-agnostic: call it from your own automation any time you need a person affiliated with an Organization. It never writes logs; it returns HasError and ErrorMessage instead.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Created when no Current affiliation was found, Updated otherwise: decided by the same lookup that made the save an update.</description>
        <name>ConversionStatusValue</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>if(IsBlank({!getCurrentAffiliation.Id}),&apos;Created&apos;,&apos;Updated&apos;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>(NPSP) Utility | Upsert | Affiliation {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <isOverridable>true</isOverridable>
    <label>(NPSP) Utility | Upsert | Affiliation</label>
